https:\/\/structural-systematicphilosophy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/470","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/structural-systematicphilosophy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/structural-systematicphilosophy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/page"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/structural-systematicphilosophy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/structural-systematicphilosophy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=470"}],"version-history":[{"count":8,"href":"https:\/\/structural-systematicphilosophy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/470\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":481,"href":"https:\/\/structural-systematicphilosophy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/470\/revisions\/481"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/structural-systematicphilosophy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=470"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}},{"id":463,"date":"2025-12-17T15:17:11","date_gmt":"2025-12-17T20:47:11","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/structural-systematicphilosophy.com\/?page_id=463"},"modified":"2025-12-17T15:43:57","modified_gmt":"2025-12-17T21:13:57","slug":"blog","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"https:\/\/structural-systematicphilosophy.com\/blog\/","title":{"rendered":"Blog"},"content":{"rendered":"\t\t<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-page\" data-elementor-id=\"463\" class=\"elementor elementor-463\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-8011001 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"8011001\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-8e3a9df elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"8e3a9df\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>Many of the posts and pages linked from here presuppose familiarity with the structural-systematic philosophy (SSP); the quickest way to develop such familiarity is to read <a href=\"http:\/\/sites.williams.edu\/awhite\/files\/2015\/05\/White-2014-TAPTOE-1-2.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">the first two chapters of my book\u00a0<em>Toward a Philosophical Theory of Everything<\/em>\u00a0(<em>TAPTOE<\/em><\/a>).<\/p><ul><li><a href=\"https:\/\/sites.williams.edu\/awhite\/files\/2019\/08\/Why-has-the-SSP-attracted-so-little-attention.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Why has the SSP received so little attention?<\/a><\/li><li><a style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, 'Noto Sans', sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Color Emoji';\" href=\"http:\/\/sites.williams.edu\/awhite\/files\/2015\/09\/For-my-fellow-philosophy-professors.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">For my fellow philosophy professors<\/a><\/li><li><a style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, 'Noto Sans', sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Color Emoji';\" href=\"https:\/\/sites.williams.edu\/awhite\/files\/2025\/04\/White-2025-Being-for-IEP-Improved.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Being for\u00a0<em>Internet Encyclopedia of Philosophy<\/em> Improved<\/a><\/li><li><a style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, 'Noto Sans', sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Color Emoji';\" href=\"https:\/\/sites.williams.edu\/awhite\/files\/2025\/02\/A-Partial-History-of-My-Work-on-the-Structural-Systematic-Philosophy-with-Lorenz-B.-Puntel-With-Particular-Emphasis-on-Being.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">White 2025 A Partial History of My Work on the Structural-Systematic Philosophy With Lorenz B. Puntel, With Particular Emphasis on Being<\/a><\/li><li>17 Sept. Emendations to &#8220;Rearticulating<span style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, 'Noto Sans', sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Color Emoji';\"> Being&#8221;<\/span><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">\u00a0(<\/span><em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Review of Metaphysics<\/em><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">, Sept. 2015)<\/span><\/li><li><a style=\"font-size: 1rem;\" href=\"https:\/\/sites.williams.edu\/awhite\/files\/2024\/02\/White-2024-Rearticulating-Being-Revised.pdf\">White 2024 &#8220;Rearticulating Being Revised&#8221;<\/a><\/li><li><a style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, 'Noto Sans', sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Color Emoji';\" href=\"https:\/\/sites.williams.edu\/awhite\/files\/2025\/03\/White-2025-Being-for-IEP-Improved.pdf\">White 2025 Being for IEP Improved<\/a><\/li><li><a style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, 'Noto Sans', sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Color Emoji';\" href=\"http:\/\/sites.williams.edu\/awhite\/files\/2015\/09\/Being-for-TAPTOE-2nd-edition.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Clarifications of\u00a0<em>TAPTOE<\/em> on being<\/a><\/li><li><a style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, 'Noto Sans', sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Color Emoji';\" href=\"https:\/\/sites.williams.edu\/awhite\/files\/2024\/03\/Lorenz-Puntels-first-four-putatively-unassailable-objections-to-my-rearticulation-of-being-and-my-responses-to-those-objections.pdf\">Lorenz B. Puntel&#8217;s first four putatively unassailable objections to my rearticulation of being and my responses to those objections<\/a><\/li><li><a style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, 'Noto Sans', sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Color Emoji';\" href=\"https:\/\/sites.williams.edu\/awhite\/files\/2024\/05\/White-2024-Lorenz-B.-Puntels-Fifth-Putatively-Unassailable-Objection-to-my-Rearticulation-of-Being-With-My-Response.pdf\">Lorenz B. Puntel&#8217;s fifth putatively unassailable objection to my rearticulations of being and my response to that objection<\/a><\/li><li><a style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, 'Noto Sans', sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Color Emoji';\" href=\"http:\/\/sites.williams.edu\/awhite\/files\/2015\/10\/TAPTOE-corrigenda5.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>TAPTOE<\/em> brief corrigenda<\/a><\/li><li><a style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, 'Noto Sans', sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Color Emoji';\" href=\"https:\/\/sites.williams.edu\/awhite\/files\/2019\/08\/A-section-by-section-summary-of-STRUCTURE-AND-BEING-1.pdf\">A section-by-section summary of\u00a0<em>Structure and Being<\/em><\/a><\/li><li><a style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, 'Noto Sans', sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Color Emoji';\" href=\"http:\/\/sites.williams.edu\/awhite\/files\/2015\/05\/SB-corrigenda.pdf\"><em>Structure and Being<\/em> corrigenda<\/a><\/li><\/ul>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Many of the posts and pages linked from here presuppose familiarity with the structural-systematic philosophy (SSP); the quickest way to develop such familiarity is to read the first two chapters of my book\u00a0Toward a Philosophical Theory of Everything\u00a0(TAPTOE). Why has the SSP received so little attention? For my fellow philosophy professors Being for\u00a0Internet Encyclopedia of [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":0,"parent":0,"menu_order":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","template":"","meta":{"footnotes":""},"class_list":["post-463","page","type-page","status-publish","hentry"],"_hostinger_reach_plugin_has_subscription_block":false,"_hostinger_reach_plugin_is_elementor":false,"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/structural-systematicphilosophy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/463","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/structural-systematicphilosophy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/structural-systematicphilosophy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/page"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/structural-systematicphilosophy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/structural-systematicphilosophy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=463"}],"version-history":[{"count":16,"href":"https:\/\/structural-systematicphilosophy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/463\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":517,"href":"https:\/\/structural-systematicphilosophy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/463\/revisions\/517"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/structural-systematicphilosophy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=463"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}},{"id":427,"date":"2025-12-17T15:03:33","date_gmt":"2025-12-17T20:33:33","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/structural-systematicphilosophy.com\/?page_id=427"},"modified":"2025-12-17T15:16:25","modified_gmt":"2025-12-17T20:46:25","slug":"home","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"https:\/\/structural-systematicphilosophy.com\/","title":{"rendered":"Home"},"content":{"rendered":"\t\t<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-page\" data-elementor-id=\"427\" class=\"elementor elementor-427\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-1abe984 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"1abe984\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-d22b033 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"d22b033\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2eb8257 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\" data-id=\"2eb8257\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"image.default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"280\" src=\"https:\/\/structural-systematicphilosophy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/White-300x280-1.jpg\" class=\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-440\" alt=\"\" \/>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-4286331 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"4286331\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-51879a6 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"51879a6\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tUntil 2003, my focus was on so-called continental philosophy; I published (among other things) <em>Absolute Knowledge. Hegel and the Problem of Metaphysics <\/em>(1983), <em>Schelling. An Introduction to the System of Freedom <\/em>(1983), and <em>Within Nietzsche&#8217;s Labyrinth <\/em>(1990). From Fall 2003 until his death in 2024, I collaborated with Lorenz B. Puntel (Professor Emeritus, Munich) on a systematic philosophy he had been working on since the late 1970s. To date, the project has resulted in the publication of two books whose English versions are <a href=\"http:\/\/www.amazon.com\/Structure-Being-Theoretical-Systematic-Philosophy\/dp\/0271033738\/ref=sr_1_2?ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1377626835&amp;sr=8-2&amp;keywords=structure+and+being\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Structure and Being<\/em><\/a>\u00a0(2008) and <em><a href=\"http:\/\/www.amazon.com\/Being-God-Systematic-Confrontation-Heidegger\/dp\/0810128535\/ref=pd_sim_sbs_b_1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Being and God<\/a>\u00a0<\/em>(2011), both by Lorenz B. Puntel, both translated by and in collaboration with me, and a third book, by Lorenz B. Puntel and translated by me,\u00a0<em>Being and Nothing<\/em> (2025). A fourth book, my <a href=\"http:\/\/www.amazon.com\/Toward-Philosophical-Theory-Everything-Structural-Systematic\/dp\/1623567181\/ref=tmm_pap_title_0?ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1383230814&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Toward a Philosophical Theory of Everything. Contributions to the Structural-Systematic Philosophy <\/em><\/a>, was published in 2014\u00a0(thanks to the title, it&#8217;s easy to refer to the book as <em>TAPTOE<\/em>). A review published in\u00a0<em>Choice<\/em> in August 2014 describes it as &#8220;a critically important work for all those deeply interested in philosophical issues and their significance for basic human concerns,&#8221; notes that it includes an &#8220;incisive critique of theories of truth currently favored in analytic philosophy,&#8221; and adds that its &#8220;critiques of philosophical views on truth, knowledge, freedom, beauty, being, and God are carefully argued, and the discussions engage with current literature.&#8221; A Portuguese translation was published in Brazil. In the academic year 2015-16, a seminar at London University focused on <em>TAPTOE<\/em>&#8216;s<em>\u00a0<\/em>rearticulation of being\u00a0\u00a0(<a href=\"https:\/\/germanphilosophy.wordpress.com\/thinking-being-2015-2016\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https:\/\/germanphilosophy.wordpress.com\/thinking-being-2015-2016\/<\/a>).\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-926bad8 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"926bad8\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-818103a e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"818103a\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-e53c63f elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"e53c63f\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tThe image on the cover is from a painting by Williams Art Professor <a href=\"http:\/\/www.barbaratakenaga.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Barbara Takenaga<\/a>; for obvious reasons, I am delighted that she allowed\u00a0me to use it. Think how the book\u00a0would look in your home or dorm room! Worth <a href=\"http:\/\/www.amazon.com\/Toward-Philosophical-Theory-Everything-Structural-Systematic\/dp\/1623567181\/ref=sr_1_1?s=books&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1426973868&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=toward+a+philosophical+theory+of+everything\">buying<\/a> for the art alone!\n\nMuch-appreciated prepublication endorsements of <em>TAPTOE<\/em> (portions of which are included on the back cover) were\u00a0provided by Professors <a href=\"http:\/\/sites.williams.edu\/awhite\/files\/2013\/11\/Cellucci-TAPTOE-endorsement.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Carlo Cellucci<\/a> of La Sapienza University, Rome, <a href=\"http:\/\/sites.williams.edu\/awhite\/files\/2013\/11\/Colapietro-TAPTOE-endorsement.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Vincent Colapietro<\/a> of Penn State University, <a href=\"http:\/\/sites.williams.edu\/awhite\/files\/2013\/12\/Baur-endorsement.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Michael Baur<\/a> of Fordham University, and <a href=\"http:\/\/sites.williams.edu\/awhite\/files\/2013\/11\/McCumber-TAPTOE-endorsement.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">John McCumber<\/a> of UCLA.\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-bd9be15 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"bd9be15\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-faecb78 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"faecb78\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-e394bc6 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\" data-id=\"e394bc6\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"image.default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https:\/\/structural-systematicphilosophy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/TAPT-cover.jpg\" data-elementor-open-lightbox=\"yes\" data-elementor-lightbox-title=\"TAPT-cover\" data-e-action-hash=\"#elementor-action%3Aaction%3Dlightbox%26settings%3DeyJpZCI6NDU2LCJ1cmwiOiJodHRwczpcL1wvc3RydWN0dXJhbC1zeXN0ZW1hdGljcGhpbG9zb3BoeS5jb21cL3dwLWNvbnRlbnRcL3VwbG9hZHNcLzIwMjVcLzEyXC9UQVBULWNvdmVyLmpwZyJ9\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img decoding=\"async\" width=\"194\" height=\"300\" src=\"https:\/\/structural-systematicphilosophy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/TAPT-cover-194x300.jpg\" class=\"attachment-medium size-medium wp-image-456\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https:\/\/structural-systematicphilosophy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/TAPT-cover-194x300.jpg 194w, https:\/\/structural-systematicphilosophy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/TAPT-cover.jpg 420w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 194px) 100vw, 194px\" \/>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-db85879 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\" data-id=\"db85879\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"image.default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https:\/\